   "text": "<<Digital Responsibility and Formal Communication>>\n\nPresident of the United States:\n\nRewrite the following: \"Them youngins be always on that damn phone\"\n\nThe use of informal language and colloquial expressions in the original sentence reflects a casual tone. To convey a more formal and respectful perspective, it is important to rephrase the statement in a manner that aligns with official communication. The sentence can be rephrased to emphasize the need for attention to digital activity without resorting to informal terms.\n\n***\n\nIn the context of modern communication, it is essential to ensure that individuals are aware of the importance of managing their digital presence. While the original sentence may have been intended to express concern, the use of informal language and expletives can be replaced with more appropriate and respectful phrasing. A formal reiteration of the concern would focus on the need for responsible usage of technology and the importance of maintaining a professional demeanor in all interactions.",
